  "narrative": "Persistence After making other configuration changes manually via a command shell over the Quick Assist connection and the initial execution of the legitimate ‘OneDriveStandaloneUpdater.exe’ binary, the attacker then executed a PowerShell command to create a service to automatically run the exploited executable. Through this remote-control session that the attacker was able to open a command shell and drop files and execute malware, deploying them from an external SharePoint file store. The registry key entries provided the IP addresses used for the command-and-control connections made by the malicious winhttp.dll code."
